@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Privacy policy for Barcode Lab, a Make Bold Spark subsite hosted at barcode.makeboldspark.com.";
    ViewData["Keywords"] = "privacy policy, barcode.makeboldspark.com, Barcode Lab, Make Bold Spark, Make Bold Solutions";
}

<article class="privacy-page">
    <header class="privacy-page__header">
        <div class="mbs-eyebrow mbs-eyebrow--brand">Privacy</div>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>
            This policy explains how Barcode Lab handles information when you visit
            <a href="@SiteBranding.SiteUrl">@SiteBranding.SiteDomain</a>.
        </p>
        <span>Last updated: August 9, 2026</span>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
            Barcode Lab is a Make Bold Spark subsite operated by Make Bold Solutions LLC.
            The site is designed as a lightweight informational and demonstration website.
            It does not require user accounts, subscriptions, or payments.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Information You Provide</h2>
        <p>
            If you use a barcode generator, sample link, upload control, or other interactive
            feature, the values you submit may be processed temporarily to render the requested
            result. Do not enter sensitive personal, financial, medical, or confidential business
            information into public demo tools.
        </p>
        <p>
            If the site later adds a contact form, email signup, or similar feature, information
            submitted through that feature will be used to respond to the request or provide the
            requested service.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Automatically Collected Information</h2>
        <p>
            Like most websites, hosting providers, security services, and server software may
            collect routine technical information such as IP address, browser type, device type,
            referring page, pages visited, request URL, and timestamps. This information is used
            to operate the site, troubleshoot issues, prevent abuse, and understand general usage.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
        <p>
            This site does not require cookies for account login or ecommerce. Some browser
            storage may be used by standard web libraries, embedded services, analytics, or user
            interface preferences if those features are enabled. You can control cookies and site
            storage through your browser settings.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Analytics and Third Parties</h2>
        <p>
            The site may use privacy-conscious analytics, hosting analytics, content delivery
            networks, font assets, or security tools. These providers may process technical data
            according to their own privacy practices. External links are provided for convenience;
            Make Bold Solutions LLC is not responsible for the privacy practices of third-party
            websites.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>How Information Is Used</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>To display pages and generate requested demo output.</li>
            <li>To maintain, secure, and improve the site.</li>
            <li>To diagnose errors, performance issues, and abuse attempts.</li>
            <li>To respond to messages if a contact method is provided.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
            Demo inputs are not intended to be stored as user records. Technical logs may be kept
            for a limited period by the application, host, or security provider for operations,
            security, and debugging. Log retention depends on the hosting and monitoring services
            in use.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Your Choices</h2>
        <p>
            You can avoid submitting personal information through demo fields, disable cookies or
            site storage in your browser, and avoid using interactive features if you do not want
            values processed by the site. Depending on your location, you may have privacy rights
            related to access, correction, deletion, or objection to certain processing.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            This site is not directed to children and does not knowingly collect personal
            information from children.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
            Reasonable technical and organizational measures are used to protect the site.
            No website or internet transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
            This policy may be updated as the site changes. The latest version will be posted on
            this page with an updated date.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Questions about this policy can be directed to
            <a href="@SiteBranding.ParentUrl">Make Bold Solutions LLC</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</article>
